content.text:
The data points to a single fault: search went away and stayed away for the whole abnormal window. I'm not running more queries, since the evidence needed is already in hand.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, count(*) n, round(avg(value),2) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.deployment.available' AND service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search deployment reports available=0 across all abnormal samples, versus 1 in normal."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "No search service spans at all in the abnormal period; normal had about 366 search server spans."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, attr_status_code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND (span_name='search.Search/Nearby' OR span_name='HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Every frontend call to search.Search/Nearby errors in about 0.02 ms, and every HTTP /hotels returns 500."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('HTTP /hotels','search.Search/Nearby') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search failure surfaces at frontend as 565 HTTP /hotels requests returning 500, all with failed search calls."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
